{"type": "message", "id": "5dfaa9cf", "parentId": "cc20a33d", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T09:09:34.747Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_Fpgp8d34fh1i9HSKD2zTLpeD", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Estimated deaths 2025 liver cancer 'Estimated Deaths in 2025' liver and intrahepatic bile duct American Cancer Society 2025 deaths\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 1003,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4fbf1b4b07e23d83\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer of the Liver and Intrahepatic Bile Duct - Cancer Stat Facts\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4fbf1b4b07e23d83\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/livibd.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"60040a828ec64584\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLiver and intrahepatic bile duct cancer represents 2.1% of all new cancer cases in the U.S. ... In 2025, it is estimated that there will be 42,240 new cases of liver and intrahepatic bile duct cancer and an estimated <strong>30,090 people</strong> will die of ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"60040a828ec64584\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seer.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4ea3b096980c903c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer statistics, 2025 - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4ea3b096980c903c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39817679/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f212f920b80de58\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe cancer mortality rate continued to decline through 2022, averting nearly <strong>4.5 million</strong> deaths since 1991 because of smoking reductions, earlier detection for some cancers, and improved treatment.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f212f920b80de58\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"618861f194ffe509\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLiver Cancer Survival Rates | American Cancer Society | American Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"618861f194ffe509\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/liver-cancer/detection-diagnosis-staging/survival-rates.html.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c9032c232f7f15b4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSurvival rates for liver cancer are based on how far the cancer has spread. Find out more about the survival rates for liver cancer.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c9032c232f7f15b4\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9b7031fca44a46b7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nKey Statistics About Liver Cancer | American Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9b7031fca44a46b7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/liver-cancer/about/what-is-key-statistics.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d431f33e705c24d2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn many of these countries it is the most common type of cancer. More than 800,000 people are diagnosed with this cancer each year throughout the world. Liver cancer is also a leading cause of cancer deaths worldwide, accounting for <strong>more than 700,000 deaths each year</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d431f33e705c24d2\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 13, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"36ecdca11271b96b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer Death Statistics in US 2025 | Key Facts - The World Data\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"36ecdca11271b96b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://theworlddata.com/cancer-death-statistics-in-us/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6d48cda5d7e30fd6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThese staggering disparities reflect geographic isolation, limited healthcare infrastructure in tribal areas, lower screening rates, and higher prevalence of risk factors including smoking, obesity, and hepatitis infections. The AI/AN population has the highest mortality rates for liver and intrahepatic bile duct cancer, followed by Hispanic/Latino and Asian/Pacific Islander populations, likely reflecting higher rates of chronic hepatitis B and C infections in these communities.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6d48cda5d7e30fd6\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 6, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"theworlddata.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4275b74fc2c64c68\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAL 30,030 AZ 42,560 AR 19,700 CA 199,980 CO 29,020 CT 23,920 DE 7,680 FL\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4275b74fc2c64c68\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/content/dam/cancer-org/research/cancer-facts-and-statistics/annual-cancer-facts-and-figures/2025/2025-cancer-facts-and-figures-acs.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2071480b87645b2e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTable 3. Estimated Number of Deaths ... US, 2025 ... Dist. of Columbia ... <strong>Estimates are rounded to nearest 10.</strong> State estimates may not sum to US total due to rounding and exclusion of state estimates of fewer than 50 deaths. Estimates are not · available for Puerto Rico.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2071480b87645b2e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_