{"type": "message", "id": "ccdb229c", "parentId": "93a80451", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T09:09:54.886Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_grqpUGV7ucQEGocy1f9gjCnK", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "leading causes of cancer deaths 2025 United States top 10 cancer deaths 2025 table 'Leading Sites of Cancer Deaths 2025 estimates' 'lung' 'colorectal' 'pancreas' 'breast' 'liver' 'prostate' 'ovarian' 'leukemia' 'brain' 'esophagus' 'stomach' 'kidney' 'uterine' 'melanoma' 'cancer deaths 2025 by site'", "count": 10}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "custom-api-shubiaobiao-cn", "model": "gpt-5-mini", "usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 0, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1775293784901, "responseId": "chatcmpl-DQrIhLaDUtUnuCLaPVOXqlVpqcVOe"}}
{"type": "message", "id": "dc770b1c", "parentId": "ccdb229c", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T09:09:55.882Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_grqpUGV7ucQEGocy1f9gjCnK", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"leading causes of cancer deaths 2025 United States top 10 cancer deaths 2025 table 'Leading Sites of Cancer Deaths 2025 estimates' 'lung' 'colorectal' 'pancreas' 'breast' 'liver' 'prostate' 'ovarian' 'leukemia' 'brain' 'esophagus' 'stomach' 'kidney' 'uterine' 'melanoma' 'cancer deaths 2025 by site'\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 994,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"162634eda0424f12\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer statistics, 2025 - PMC - NIH\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"162634eda0424f12\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11745215/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"abbee9e0b80c3c2d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAIAN people have the highest cancer mortality of any group for cancers of the colorectum, kidney, liver, lung, stomach, and cervix. Black men have the highest prostate cancer mortality, from two‐fold to four‐fold that in any other group, whereas Black women have the highest breast and uterine corpus cancer mortality, with the latter from two‐fold to three‐fold that of all other women.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"abbee9e0b80c3c2d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ab183bdf97f8d9bb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer statistics, 2025 - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ab183bdf97f8d9bb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39817679/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1be7f0b3cef02958\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nYet alarming disparities persist; Native American people bear the highest cancer mortality, including rates that are two to three times those in White people for kidney, liver, stomach, and cervical cancers. Similarly, Black people have two-fold higher mortality than White people for prostate, stomach, and uterine corpus cancers.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1be7f0b3cef02958\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ce815cc0eb75befe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer Facts & Figures 2025 | American Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ce815cc0eb75befe\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/research/cancer-facts-statistics/all-cancer-facts-figures/2025-cancer-facts-figures.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ecfab66a6917ae1c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe 2025 annual report provides estimated numbers of new cancer cases, deaths, survivors and statistics on prevention, early detection, and treatment.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ecfab66a6917ae1c\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d2feea0be85d063f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer Stat Facts: Common Cancer Sites - SEER\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d2feea0be85d063f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/common.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f18d643c28d45953\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>Lung and bronchus cancer</strong> is responsible for the most deaths with 124,730 people expected to die from this disease. That is nearly three times the 52,900 deaths due to colorectal cancer, which is the second most common cause of cancer death.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f18d643c28d45953\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seer.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"06b36ff39817242c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer statistics, 2025 - Siegel - 2025 - CA: A Cancer Journal for Clinicians - Wiley Online Library\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"06b36ff39817242c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://acsjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.3322/caac.21871\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8689847bab194e6d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAIAN people have the highest cancer mortality of any group for cancers of the colorectum, kidney, liver, lung, stomach, and cervix. Black men have the highest prostate cancer mortality, from two-fold to four-fold that in any other group, whereas Black women have the highest breast and uterine corpus cancer mortality, with the latter from two-fold to three-fold that of all other women.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8689847bab194e6d\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 16, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"acsjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fe345edac9fbb429\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2025 Cancer Statistics Report: Lung Cancer Remains Leading Cause of Cancer Mortality in US\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fe345edac9fbb429\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.lungcancerstoday.com/post/2025-cancer-statistics-report-lung-cancer-remains-leading-cause-of-cancer-mortality-in-us\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bce677827e6c2d75\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAlthough <strong>lung cancer</strong> incidence is declining and five-year survival rates are increasing, <strong>lung cancer</strong> remains the top cause of cancer mortality in the United States, causing nearly 2.5 times